==Background==
[[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] reached their second FIFA Club World Cup Final in two appearances, having done so previously in [[2012 FIFA Club World Cup Final|2012]], which they lost to [[Sport Club Corinthians Paulista|Corinthians]]. Chelsea were looking to win their second title of the season, after the [[2021 UEFA Super Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Lukaku goal sends Chelsea to the final |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/60307726 |access-date=10 February 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Romelu Lukaku's first-half strike sends Blues into Club World Cup final |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/al-hilal-vs-chelsea/report/460725 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=10 February 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

[[Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras|Palmeiras]] were competing in the FIFA Club World Cup for the second consecutive time, having finished fourth in [[2020 FIFA Club World Cup|2020]]. They reached the final for the first time after defeating [[Al Ahly SC|Al Ahly]], who had previously defeated them in the third place playoff in 2020.<ref>{{cite web |title=Veiga, Dudu propel Palmeiras into final |url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/clubworldcup/uae2021/news/fifa-club-world-cup-2021-matchday-three-review-palmeiras-al-ahly |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |website=FIFA.com |access-date=10 February 2022 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Palmeiras beat Al Ahly to reach Club World Cup final |url=https://www.espn.com/football/report/_/gameId/622404 |website=ESPN |access-date=10 February 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

This was the fourth FIFA Club World Cup Final to be played between English and Brazilian clubs, after [[2005 FIFA Club World Championship Final|2005]], [[2012 FIFA Club World Cup Final|2012]] and  [[2019 FIFA Club World Cup Final|2019]], with only the latter being won by the English club.<ref>{{cite news |title=The FIFA Club World Cup final in stats |url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/clubworldcup/uae2021/news/the-fifa-club-world-cup-final-in-stats |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |access-date=12 February 2022 |language=en |archive-date=12 February 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220212024200/https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/clubworldcup/uae2021/news/the-fifa-club-world-cup-final-in-stats |url-status=dead }}</ref>

