===Chelsea===
Chelsea qualified for the tournament as the champions of the [[2020–21 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]], having defeated fellow English club [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] in the [[2021 UEFA Champions League Final|final]]. Due to their participation in the Club World Cup, two of their [[Premier League]] fixtures were rescheduled.<ref>{{cite web |title=Two games postponed due to Club World Cup participation |url=https://www.chelseafc.com/en/news/2021/11/30/two-games-postponed-due-to-club-world-cup-participation |publisher=Chelsea Football Club |access-date=12 February 2022}}</ref>

As European champions, Chelsea received a bye to the semi-finals, where they faced [[Asian Football Confederation|Asian]] champions [[Al Hilal SFC|Al Hilal]] from Saudi Arabia. The Blues won the match 1–0; [[Romelu Lukaku]] scored the only goal of the game in the 32nd minute.<ref>{{cite news |title=Lukaku goal sends Chelsea to the final |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/60307726 |access-date=12 February 2022 |work=BBC Sport}}</ref>

===Palmeiras===
Palmeiras entered the tournament as the winners of the [[2021 Copa Libertadores|Copa Libertadores]], defeating another Brazilian club [[Clube de Regatas do Flamengo|Flamengo]] after [[Overtime (sports)|extra time]] in the [[2021 Copa Libertadores Final|final]], which took place a few days before the draw for the Club World Cup.<ref>{{cite news |title=Palmeiras see off Flamengo in extra time to retain Copa Libertadores title |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/nov/27/palmeiras-flamengo-copa-libertadores-final-match-report |access-date=12 February 2022 |work=The Guardian |date=27 November 2021 |language=en}}</ref>

Palmeiras too entered the Club World Cup in the semi-finals stage, where they played [[Confederation of African Football|African]] champions [[Al Ahly SC|Al Ahly]] of Egypt. Palmeiras won the match 2–0 with goals from [[Raphael Veiga]] and [[Dudu (footballer, born 1992)|Dudu]], their first goals in the Club World Cup.<ref>{{cite news |title=Palmeiras beat Al Ahly to reach Club World Cup final |url=https://www.reuters.com/lifestyle/sports/palmeiras-beat-al-ahly-reach-club-world-cup-final-2022-02-08/ |access-date=12 February 2022 |work=Reuters |date=8 February 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

